    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled along the ever-popular Moyne Road, this attractive four-bedroom end-of-terrace period redbrick residence presents a wonderful opportunity to create a truly exceptional family home in one of Dublin's most sought-after neighbourhoods. Behind its charming brick façade and railed front garden lies a property brimming with character and untapped potential. While in need of refurbishment, the house retains many original period features and offers generous proportions throughout, providing the perfect canvas for those eager to restore and modernise to their own taste and specification.\nAs an end-of-terrace home, the property benefits from valuable side access — ideal for bicycles, bins, or future landscaping plans — and enjoys a sense of light and space not often found. To the rear, a generous garden offers excellent scope for extension (subject to planning permission) while still leaving ample outdoor space for family living and entertaining. The front garden, neatly railed, adds to the home's classic appeal, while ample on-street parking ensures convenience for residents and visitors alike\nMoyne Road enjoys a prime position just moments from Dunville Avenue's selection of artisan shops, cafés, and everyday conveniences. Ranelagh & Rathmines Villages are within strolling distance, offering a vibrant mix of restaurants, boutiques, and lively social spots. Beechwood LUAS provides swift access to the city centre, while Grafton Street and Dundrum Town Centre are both easily accessible for shopping and entertainment. The area is renowned for its excellent schools, making this an ideal choice for families seeking a long-term home in a thriving community.\nThis is a rare chance to acquire a substantial period property in a premier location and transform it into a bespoke residence tailored to modern living. With its classic architecture, side access, generous gardens, and exceptional amenities on the doorstep, this Moyne Road home truly oozes potential.\nViewing comes highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 6.9m x 2m\n\n\nLiving Room - 4.34m x 3.80m\n\n\nFamily Room - 4.18m x 3.35m\n\n\nKitchen - 2.39m x 2.03m\n\n\nDining Room - 3.37m x 3.32m\n\n\nBathroom - 3.92m x 1.41m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.86m x 3.39m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.11m x 3.44m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.89m x 2.57m\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.25m x 3.02m\n\n\nBathroom - 2m x 1.73m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Superb, four bedroom redbrick family home</li><li> Charming, characterful property with many period features</li><li> Wonderful Ranelagh location</li><li> Close to Dunville avenue and Ranelagh main street</li><li> Close to Beechwood LUAS stop</li><li> Ample on street parking</li><li> Gated side entrance</li><li> Potential to extend (stpp)</ul>"
